siotherapist and senior researcher at Ariel University, is one of the world's leading experts in the field of Rett Syndrome treatment with over 30 years of clinical and research experience. His scientific output includes 38 focused articles on Rett Syndrome with over 1,200 citations in total, indicating his significant influence in this field.\" — Topic content - knowledge base text for AI reference. May be empty if topic is just a category.\n      - subtopics: {map} — Nested subtopics under this topic. View to see available subtopics. \n          (may contain items - view \"/Context_Library/A comprehensive list of articles on Rett Syndrome by Prof. Meir Lotan/subtopics\" to load from database)\n      - active: (not in schema)\n      ↪ To expand: view \"/Context_Library/A comprehensive list of articles on Rett Syndrome by Prof. Meir Lotan/*\". (read-only)\n  - Physiotherapy Goals - Gross Motor Skills: {object}\n      - id: \"f0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001\" — Topic UUID (for internal reference)\n      - title: \"Physiotherapy Goals - Gross Motor Skills\" — Topic title\n      - content: \"Individual Physiotherapy Learning Plans (תוכנית לימוד אישית - פיזיותרפיה) for pediatric gross motor development. These structured therapy goal templates are used in Israeli special education (TALA) settings for children with motor development needs. Each goal includes: Long-term objectives, intervention methods, prerequisites/conditions, success criteria, and designated implementers (physiotherapist and/or educational team).\" — Topic content - knowledge base text for AI reference. May be empty if topic is just a category.\n      - subtopics: {map} — Nested subtopics under this topic. View to see available subtopics. \n          (may contain items - view \"/Context_Library/Physiotherapy Goals - Gross Motor Skills/subtopics\" to load from database)\n      - active: (not in schema)\n      ↪ To expand: view \"/Context_Library/Physiotherapy Goals - Gross Motor Skills/*\". (read-on